WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.993 --> 00:00:16.175
grinned proudly as Rann flew off.

2
00:00:16.195 --> 00:00:19.378
"Mowgli remembered the hawk's language!

3
00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:22.901
And he found a way to send us a message."

4
00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:25.603
"See?" Bagheera said.

5
00:00:25.623 --> 00:00:28.565
"I told you that he's very smart.

6
00:00:29.046 --> 00:00:31.368
But we'd better get to Monkey City right away."

7
00:00:32.748 --> 00:00:37.351
Everyone knew where Monkey City was, but few jungle animals went there.

8
00:00:39.953 --> 00:00:43.416
It was an old deserted city, buried in the jungle.

9
00:00:44.697 --> 00:00:48.319
Only the monkeys liked to use places once used by people.

10
00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:56.125
"It is half a night's journey—at full speed," Bagheera said, glancing at the old bear.

11
00:00:56.145 --> 00:01:00.468
"I'll go as fast as I can," Baloo promised.

12
00:01:01.404 --> 00:01:03.606
"We can't wait for you," Bagheera said.

13
00:01:03.626 --> 00:01:05.687
"Kaa and I will rush ahead.

14
00:01:06.087 --> 00:01:07.769
You can follow as best you can."

15
00:01:09.029 --> 00:01:11.671
"I have no feet," Kaa said.

16
00:01:11.691 --> 00:01:14.433
"But I'm very fast.

17
00:01:14.913 --> 00:01:15.614
Let's go."

18
00:01:18.256 --> 00:01:23.139
Baloo hurried after Kaa and Bagheera, but soon he stopped, panting.

19
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:29.844
Bagheera kept running, while Kaa seemed to pour himself along the ground.

20
00:01:33.184 --> 00:01:38.046
The snake found the quickest route through the jungle with his steady eyes and followed it.

21
00:01:43.348 --> 00:01:45.469
Mowgli looked around Monkey City.

22
00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:47.750
It was in ruins now.

23
00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.991
But some king had built it long ago.

24
00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:57.554
Trees grew in and out of marble walls, and wild vines hung from windows.

25
00:01:58.615 --> 00:02:01.576
There was a palace with no roof at the top of the hill.

26
00:02:02.464 --> 00:02:06.045
Below the palace were rows of houses and empty pits.

27
00:02:06.805 --> 00:02:09.646
Shattered domes from temples lay on the ground.

28
00:02:12.327 --> 00:02:14.888
The monkeys called this place Monkey City.

29
00:02:15.588 --> 00:02:18.989
Yet they had no idea how to use the people's buildings.

30
00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:24.330
They sat inside the marble rooms and scratched for fleas.

31
00:02:25.351 --> 00:02:29.932
They raced along the terrace, shaking orange trees, just to watch the fruit fall.

32
00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.305
They drank and fought at the water tanks.

33
00:02:34.965 --> 00:02:38.226
Every once in a while, the monkeys got tired of the city.

34
00:02:39.066 --> 00:02:41.247
Then they went back to the treetops.

35
00:02:44.148 --> 00:02:46.569
The monkeys reached the city late in the day.

36
00:02:47.229 --> 00:02:53.291
Instead of going to sleep after the long journey, the monkeys joined hands and danced.

37
00:02:54.691 --> 00:02:56.912
One monkey even made a long speech.

38
00:02:59.284 --> 00:03:03.186
"This man cub is going to change monkey history!"

39
00:03:03.646 --> 00:03:04.326
he announced.

40
00:03:05.007 --> 00:03:08.108
"This boy will show us how to weave sticks together.

41
00:03:08.568 --> 00:03:10.249
We can create shelters."

42
00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.472
With a sigh, Mowgli began to weave some sticks together.

43
00:03:18.032 --> 00:03:20.934
A few monkeys tried to do just what he was doing.

44
00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:26.056
But one by one, they got bored and jumped up.

45
00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.082
Some started pulling friends' tails.

46
00:03:30.003 --> 00:03:31.664
Others jumped around, singing.

47
00:03:33.005 --> 00:03:36.128
Finally Mowgli gave up and put down the sticks.

48
00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:37.890
"I'm hungry!"

49
00:03:39.011 --> 00:03:41.673
Twenty monkeys jumped up to bring him nuts.

50
00:03:42.974 --> 00:03:46.777
They started fighting on the way—and forgot all about the food.

51
00:03:46.797 --> 00:03:50.641
"Baloo was right," Mowgli thought.

52
00:03:51.341 --> 00:03:54.124
"Monkeys have no laws and no leader.

53
00:03:54.728 --> 00:03:57.089
All they do is steal and sing.

54
00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:58.770
I'm going home!"

55
00:03:59.991 --> 00:04:02.892
Mowgli jumped to his feet and headed toward the gate.

56
00:04:05.253 --> 00:04:07.254
But the monkeys quickly pulled him back.

57
00:04:07.274 --> 00:04:09.135
"Oh no!

58
00:04:09.295 --> 00:04:10.616
You're staying with us!"

59
00:04:11.496 --> 00:04:12.997
"Why do you want to leave?"

60
00:04:13.437 --> 00:04:14.217
a monkey said.

61
00:04:14.237 --> 00:04:17.199
"We're the most wonderful creatures in the jungle.

62
00:04:17.379 --> 00:04:19.800
We'll tell you all about how great we are!"

63
00:04:22.076 --> 00:04:26.199
All the monkeys were gathering on the terrace to listen to the silly stories.

64
00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.162
Mowgli couldn't help laughing.

65
00:04:33.445 --> 00:04:35.907
wonder if they ever sleep," he thought.

66
00:04:36.828 --> 00:04:40.091
He looked up to see a cloud sliding toward the moon.

67
00:04:41.091 --> 00:04:43.533
Soon it would be completely dark.

68
00:04:44.754 --> 00:04:46.616
He'd try again to escape then.
